{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792401867,"nonce":"uH5gLNfCTx2O7bHEe8RrX28Z8uM=","title":"Built-in extensions in RayScript: runtime, editor services, and Git first (plan)","message":"Goal: features that are not core to the editor ship as extensions written in RayScript, in the same format a user's extension has. Git is first because it needs native FFI (libgit2), the editor services an SCM needs, and a runtime that runs extensions in every project. Child issues: runtime, FFI (rayscript tracker), Git.\n\n\n- RayDE runs one extension per project: the one a `.rayext` project opens, in the Extension Studio (a development tool). Installed extensions (`.rayde/extensions`, `~/.rayde/extensions`) are only listed on the Extensions page (\"does not run extensions yet\").\n- Host process: `rayscript-host`, one per extension, JSON lines on stdio. Editor services reach scripts as remote modules; only `rayde.workspace` exists (`readFile`, `writeFile`, `activeFile`, `openFile`, `root`).\n- Hooks: `project.opened`, `active.changed`, `file.opened`, `file.closed`, `file.changed`, `file.saved`. Menus: `explorer/context`, `editor/title`. Views: `sidebar`, `secondary`, `panel`, `editor` locations, drawn from RayScript markup.\n- Capabilities: `workspace.read` and `workspace.write` are backed. `process.spawn`, `net.fetch`, `terminal`, `clipboard` are recorded and not acted on.\n- RayScript native FFI: `native \"lib\" { function f(a:Int):Int; }` parses and compiles to `BindNative`, which fails with \"native libraries are not available yet\". The VM has no bytes type. `HostObj` holds a `Box\u003cdyn Any\u003e` that is dropped when the collector sweeps it, which can be a finalizer.\n- ashui has gutter markers, line decorations, a code editor, pooled rows, popovers. RayDE has the Prompt component, a status bar, Explorer rows, an Output panel.\n- libgit2 is not installed here; cmake and a network are. The `git` CLI is 2.50.\n\n\nA built-in is a folder `extensions/\u003cid\u003e/` in the RayDE repo: `\u003cid\u003e.rayext`, `ext/*.rays`, `natives/` for libraries. It is packaged with the app. Differences from a user extension: pre-approved capabilities and native libraries, not removable, shown as built-in.\n\nAn extension manager in RayDE (child issue 1) discovers built-in, user and workspace extensions, activates them on events (`onStartup`, `workspaceContains:\u003cfile\u003e`, `onCommand:\u003cid\u003e`), runs each in its own host process, merges their contributions (commands, menus, views in the activity bar, settings sections, key bindings), and restarts one that exits. The Studio becomes the development view of one running extension.\n\nGit talks to libgit2 through RayScript FFI (child issue 2) in its host process: a native fault kills that host, RayDE restarts it and reports it in the Output channel.\n\n\nM0 Extension manager. Exit: the Markdown preview fixture runs from `.rayde/extensions` in a Haxe project, two extensions run side by side, an extension that exits is restarted, disabled extensions do not start.\nM1 FFI in rayscript, in parallel with M0. Exit: a fixture cdylib exercises every type class on macOS arm64; libgit2 opens a repository from a script.\nM2 Git, read only. Repository discovery, status (staged, unstaged, untracked, conflicted), branch and ahead/behind, an SCM view in the sidebar, Explorer badges, editor gutter changes against the index and HEAD, status bar item, an open-changes diff tab. Refresh on `file.saved`, `active.changed`, window focus and watcher events for `.git/index`, `.git/HEAD`, `.git/refs`.\nM3 Git, local writes. Stage and unstage a file, discard (with confirmation), commit (message prompt, amend, sign-off setting, pre-commit, commit-msg and post-commit hooks run through `process.spawn`, because libgit2 does not run hooks), create, switch and delete branches, stash, init. Hunk staging after the diff view has hunks.\nM4 Remotes. Fetch, pull, push with progress in the status bar; credentials: ssh through ssh-agent, https through `git credential fill`.\nM5 History. Log and graph view (revwalk), file history, blame (inline and gutter), compare refs, tags. Interactive rebase, cherry-pick UI and signing stay on the `git` CLI through `process.spawn`.\n\n\n- `rayde.window`: `showMessage(kind, text, actions)`, `prompt(options)`, `confirm(text, buttons)`, `progress(title, task)`; `rayde.output.channel(name)`.\n- `rayde.statusbar.item(id, {text, icon, tooltip, command, side, priority})`.\n- `rayde.explorer.decorate(path, {badge, color, tooltip})` with batching; Explorer rows take a decoration.\n- `rayde.editor.markers(path, owner, [{line, kind}])` onto ashui gutter markers; `rayde.editor.decorate` for inline blame.\n- `rayde.fs.watch(patterns, handler)`, implemented in the host (Rust `notify`), debounced.\n- Capability `process.spawn` with an allow-list per extension, and a `native:\u003clibrary\u003e` capability.\n- Contributions: `contributes.configuration` (schema rendered in the extension's settings section), `contributes.keybindings`, menu locations `scm/title`, `scm/resource/context`, `status`.\n- A diff view: first as a read-only CodeEditor with added/removed line decorations (unified); side by side later, possibly an ashui component.\n\n\n- FFI: fixture cdylib in rayscript tests; Git: a scripted repository fixture in RayDE (`tests/fixtures/git`), checks for the model, a snapshot scenario `git` (SCM view, gutter, commit, branch switch, conflict, diff tab) feeding a `docs/git.md` chapter with its screenshots.\n- Status on a repository of 10k files stays off the UI thread (worker lane) and is benchmarked; refresh is incremental.\n- Every extension registers a `describe` command that returns structured state (for Git: repository, branch, counts, last error) for agents and for the Extensions page.\n\n\n- Callbacks from a worker thread into the VM thread, finalizer order (objects before their repository), libgit2 thread safety, Windows x64 calling convention, extension start-up cost.\n- libgit2 runs no hooks, no gpg signing, no interactive rebase: the `git` CLI is a deliberate partner for those.\n\n\n1. libgit2 over FFI as the engine, CLI through `process.spawn` for hooks, rebase and signing.\n2. FFI engine: `libloading` + `libffi` crates in rayscript-vm (calls and closures for any signature), over a hand-rolled caller and trampoline pool. rayscript has no external dependencies today.\n3. libgit2 vendored (pinned release, checksum) and built with cmake into `natives/` by a script, `USE_SSH=exec`.\n4. SCM view in RayScript first, with a data model that can move to a host-drawn view if row counts demand it.\n5. Built-ins live in the RayDE repo under `extensions/`.\n\nAfter Git: promote the Markdown preview to a built-in, then candidates: TODO tree, JSON and CSS tools, Haxe tasks.","files":null}]}